Database migrations (SQLite)
===========================

Run these commands from src/v1 with the project's virtual environment active.
Configure src/.env first. DATABASE_URL overrides the default src/v1/demo.db.

Initialize a fresh database or apply pending migrations:

    python -m alembic upgrade head
    python -m alembic check

After editing the SQLAlchemy models, generate and review a new migration:

    python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
    python -m alembic upgrade head
    python -m alembic check

Migrations create schema only. The application adds demo data on its first
startup with an empty database, unless DEMO_DATA=false is set in src/.env.

Migration history was consolidated on 2026-11-11. The complete initial schema
retains revision 9b7c4e2a61d0, the former development head. Databases already at
that revision skip the initial migration and apply newer migrations normally.
For a database on an earlier revision, back it up and upgrade it using the old
migration files from Git history before using this consolidated history. Do not
stamp an older database
as current without checking and applying the actual schema changes.

Downgrading this initial migration to base removes ALL application tables and
their data. Use downgrade base only on disposable databases. The automated
migration test checks upgrade/check/downgrade/re-upgrade on a temporary database.
